                  "index": 0,
                  "text": "The user wants a two-sentence summary of Hamlet's plot. Let me think about the key elements:\n\n1. Prince Hamlet of Denmark learns from his father's ghost that his uncle Claudius murdered his father and has since married Hamlet's mother Gertrude and taken the throne.\n2. Hamlet feigns madness (or is it real?) while seeking revenge, his hesitation and actions lead to a cascade of deaths including Ophelia, Polonius, Laertes, Gertrude, Rosencrantz and Guildenstern, and ultimately himself and Claudius.\n\nI need to condense this into exactly two sentences. Let me draft:\n\nSentence 1: Set up the premise - ghost reveals murder, Claudius's guilt.\nSentence 2: The consequences - Hamlet's quest for revenge (and delay) ends in tragedy with nearly everyone dead.\n\nDraft:\n\"Prince Hamlet of Denmark is visited by the ghost of his father, who reveals that he was murdered by his own brother Claudius, who has since seized the throne and married Hamlet's mother, Gertrude. Consumed by grief and a desire for revenge, Hamlet feigns madness while delaying action, ultimately triggering a chain of deaths—including his love Ophelia, her father Polonius, and finally his mother, Laertes, and Claudius himself, who all perish in the tragedy's final duel alongside Hamlet.\"\n\nThat's a bit long. Let me tighten:\n\n\"Prince Hamlet of Denmark is visited by his father's ghost, who reveals that Hamlet's uncle Claudius murdered the king to seize the throne and marry Hamlet's mother Gertrude. Feigning madness as he struggles to avenge his father, Hamlet's hesitation and schemes set off a chain of tragic deaths, culminating in a final duel in which Gertrude, Claudius, Laertes, and Hamlet himself all perish.\"\n\nThat's good - two sentences, captures the essential plot: the ghost's revelation, the setup, the revenge plot, and the tragic ending. Format should be just the two sentences, perhaps with a very brief intro or not at all. The user asked for exactly two sentences, so I should deliver just that - maybe no preamble needed, or a minimal one. I'll just give the two sentences cleanly.",
